{"pageProps":{"metadata":{"homepage":"https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless","maintainers":[{"email":"appu@google.com","github":"loosebazooka","name":"Appu Goundan","github_user_id":1304826},{"email":"sahin@aspect.dev","github":"thesayyn","name":"Şahin Yort","github_user_id":20563340}],"repository":["github:bazel-contrib/rules_distroless"],"versions":["0.1.2","0.1.3","0.1.8","0.2.0","0.2.1","0.3.0","0.3.1","0.3.2","0.3.3","0.3.7","0.3.8","0.4.0","0.4.1","0.4.2","0.5.1","0.5.3","0.6.1"],"yanked_versions":{}},"versionInfos":[{"version":"0.6.1","submission":{"status":["A"],"files":["modules/rules_distroless/0.6.1/source.json"],"hash":"8ad160ecc2b7b43d1ddfc822816ec82c0a5890a5","authorDate":"2025-10-24 18:58:53 -0700","authorDateRel":"7 weeks ago","authorDateIso":"2025-10-25T01:58:53Z"},"moduleInfo":{"compatibilityLevel":1,"dependencies":[{"module":"platforms","dev":false,"version":"0.0.10"},{"module":"bazel_features","dev":false,"version":"1.20.0"},{"module":"bazel_lib","dev":false,"version":"3.0.0-rc.0"},{"module":"bazel_skylib","dev":false,"version":"1.5.0"},{"module":"rules_java","dev":false,"version":"8.8.0"},{"module":"rules_shell","dev":false,"version":"0.4.1"},{"module":"gawk","dev":false,"version":"5.3.2.bcr.3"},{"module":"tar.bzl","dev":false,"version":"0.6.0"},{"module":"yq.bzl","dev":false,"version":"0.3.1"},{"module":"gazelle","dev":true,"version":"0.34.0"},{"module":"bazel_skylib_gazelle_plugin","dev":true,"version":"1.5.0"},{"module":"buildifier_prebuilt","dev":true,"version":"8.0.1"},{"module":"rules_oci","dev":true,"version":"2.0.0"},{"module":"container_structure_test","dev":true,"version":"1.21.1"},{"module":"jq.bzl","dev":true,"version":"0.4.0"}],"supportedPlatforms":["debian10","macos","ubuntu2004"],"supportedBazelVersions":["7.x","8.x"]},"isYanked":false,"yankReason":null,"hasAttestationFile":true,"sourceJson":{"integrity":"sha256-lZ6hZtUWGDQpK9ekPu/QOFV4tpq4VkHLoOJ5r6dH+TM=","strip_prefix":"rules_distroless-0.6.1","docs_url":"https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/releases/download/v0.6.1/rules_distroless-v0.6.1.docs.tar.gz","url":"https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/releases/download/v0.6.1/rules_distroless-v0.6.1.tar.gz","patches":{"module_dot_bazel_version.patch":"sha256-2t8FL947yXGa5vTTYltp/0cPdsHSQgm9Jgm44+lzGjU="},"patch_strip":1},"stardocs":[{"ruleInfo":[],"providerInfo":[],"funcInfo":[{"functionName":"apt.install","parameter":[{"name":"name","docString":"name of the repository","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"manifest","docString":"label to a `manifest.yaml`","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"lock","docString":"label to a `lock.json`","defaultValue":"None","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"nolock","docString":"bool, set to True if you explicitly want to run without a lock\nand avoid the DEBUG messages.","defaultValue":"False","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"package_template","docString":"(EXPERIMENTAL!) a template file for generated BUILD\nfiles. Available template replacement keys are:\n`{target_name}`, `{deps}`, `{urls}`, `{name}`,\n`{arch}`, `{sha256}`, `{repo_name}`","defaultValue":"None","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"resolve_transitive","docString":"whether dependencies of dependencies should be\nresolved and added to the lockfile.","defaultValue":"True","mandatory":false,"role":0}],"docString":"Repository macro to create Debian repositories.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> THIS IS A LEGACY MACRO. Use it only if you are still using `WORKSPACE`.\n> Otherwise please use the [`apt` module extension](apt.md).\n\nHere's an example to create a Debian repo with `apt.install`:\n\n```starlark\n# WORKSPACE\n\nload(\"@rules_distroless//apt:apt.bzl\", \"apt\")\n\napt.install(\n    name = \"bullseye\",\n    # lock = \"//examples/apt:bullseye.lock.json\",\n    manifest = \"//examples/apt:bullseye.yaml\",\n)\n\nload(\"@bullseye//:packages.bzl\", \"bullseye_packages\")\nbullseye_packages()\n```\n\nNote that, for the initial setup (or if we want to run without a lock) the\nlockfile attribute can be omitted. All you need is a YAML\n[manifest](/examples/debian_snapshot/bullseye.yaml):\n```yaml\nversion: 1\n\nsources:\n  - channel: bullseye main\n    url: https://snapshot-cloudflare.debian.org/archive/debian/20240210T223313Z\n\narchs:\n  - amd64\n\npackages:\n  - perl\n```\n\n`apt.install` will parse the manifest and will fetch and install the\npackages for the given architectures in the Bazel repo `@<NAME>`.\n\nEach `<PACKAGE>/<ARCH>` has two targets that match the usual structure of a\nDebian package: `data` and `control`.\n\nYou can use the package like so: `@<REPO>//<PACKAGE>/<ARCH>:<TARGET>`.\n\nE.g. for the previous example, you could use `@bullseye//perl/amd64:data`.\n\n### Lockfiles\n\nAs mentioned, the macro can be used without a lock because the lock will be\ngenerated internally on-demand. However, this comes with the cost of\nperforming a new package resolution on repository cache misses.\n\nThe lockfile can be generated by running `bazel run @bullseye//:lock`. This\nwill generate a `.lock.json` file of the same name and in the same path as\nthe YAML `manifest` file.\n\nIf you explicitly want to run without a lock and avoid the warning messages\nset the `nolock` argument to `True`.\n\n### Best Practice: use snapshot archive URLs\n\nWhile we strongly encourage users to check in the generated lockfile, it's\nnot always possible because Debian repositories are rolling by default.\nTherefore, a lockfile generated today might not work later if the upstream\nrepository removes or publishes a new version of a package.\n\nTo avoid this problems and increase the reproducibility it's recommended to\navoid using normal Debian mirrors and use snapshot archives instead.\n\nSnapshot archives provide a way to access Debian package mirrors at a point\nin time. Basically, it's a \"wayback machine\" that allows access to (almost)\nall past and current packages based on dates and version numbers.\n\nDebian has had snapshot archives for [10+\nyears](https://lists.debian.org/debian-announce/2010/msg00002.html). Ubuntu\nbegan providing a similar service recently and has packages available since\nMarch 1st 2023.\n\nTo use this services simply use a snapshot URL in the manifest. Here's two\nexamples showing how to do this for Debian and Ubuntu:\n  * [/examples/debian_snapshot](/examples/debian_snapshot)\n  * [/examples/ubuntu_snapshot](/examples/ubuntu_snapshot)\n\nFor more infomation, please check https://snapshot.debian.org and/or\nhttps://snapshot.ubuntu.com.\n","originKey":{"name":"_apt_install","file":"//apt:apt.bzl"}}],"aspectInfo":[],"moduleDocstring":"`apt.install` macro\n\nThis documentation provides an overview of the convenience `apt.install`\nrepository macro to create Debian repositories with packages \"installed\" in\nthem and available to use in Bazel.","file":"//apt:apt.bzl","moduleExtensionInfo":[],"repositoryRuleInfo":[],"macroInfo":[]},{"ruleInfo":[{"ruleName":"dpkg_status","docString":"TODO: docs","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"controls","docString":"","type":7,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"dpkg_status","file":"//apt/private:dpkg_status.bzl"}},{"ruleName":"dpkg_statusd","docString":"TODO: docs","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"package_name","docString":"","type":4,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"control","docString":"","type":3,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"compression","docString":"Compress the archive file with a supported algorithm.","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"dpkg_statusd","file":"//apt/private:dpkg_statusd.bzl"}}],"providerInfo":[],"funcInfo":[],"aspectInfo":[],"moduleDocstring":"EXPERIMENTAL! Public API","file":"//apt:defs.bzl","moduleExtensionInfo":[],"repositoryRuleInfo":[],"macroInfo":[]},{"ruleInfo":[],"providerInfo":[],"funcInfo":[],"aspectInfo":[],"moduleDocstring":"apt extensions","file":"//apt:extensions.bzl","moduleExtensionInfo":[{"extensionName":"apt","docString":"","tagClass":[{"tagName":"install","docString":"Module extension to create Debian repositories.\n\nCreate Debian repositories with packages \"installed\" in them and available\nto use in Bazel.\n\n\nHere's an example how to create a Debian repo:\n\n```starlark\napt = use_extension(\"@rules_distroless//apt:extensions.bzl\", \"apt\")\napt.install(\n    name = \"bullseye\",\n    lock = \"//examples/apt:bullseye.lock.json\",\n    manifest = \"//examples/apt:bullseye.yaml\",\n)\nuse_repo(apt, \"bullseye\")\n```\n\nNote that, for the initial setup (or if we want to run without a lock) the\nlockfile attribute can be omitted. All you need is a YAML\n[manifest](/examples/debian_snapshot/bullseye.yaml):\n```yaml\nversion: 1\n\nsources:\n  - channel: bullseye main\n    url: https://snapshot-cloudflare.debian.org/archive/debian/20240210T223313Z\n\narchs:\n  - amd64\n\npackages:\n  - perl\n```\n\n`apt.install` will parse the manifest and will fetch and install the packages\nfor the given architectures in the Bazel repo `@<NAME>`.\n\nEach `<PACKAGE>/<ARCH>` has two targets that match the usual structure of a\nDebian package: `data` and `control`.\n\nYou can use the package like so: `@<REPO>//<PACKAGE>/<ARCH>:<TARGET>`.\n\nE.g. for the previous example, you could use `@bullseye//perl/amd64:data`.\n\n### Lockfiles\n\nAs mentioned, the macro can be used without a lock because the lock will be\ngenerated internally on-demand. However, this comes with the cost of\nperforming a new package resolution on repository cache misses.\n\nThe lockfile can be generated by running `bazel run @bullseye//:lock`. This\nwill generate a `.lock.json` file of the same name and in the same path as\nthe YAML `manifest` file.\n\nIf you explicitly want to run without a lock and avoid the warning messages\nset the `nolock` argument to `True`.\n\n### Best Practice: use snapshot archive URLs\n\nWhile we strongly encourage users to check in the generated lockfile, it's\nnot always possible because Debian repositories are rolling by default.\nTherefore, a lockfile generated today might not work later if the upstream\nrepository removes or publishes a new version of a package.\n\nTo avoid this problems and increase the reproducibility it's recommended to\navoid using normal Debian mirrors and use snapshot archives instead.\n\nSnapshot archives provide a way to access Debian package mirrors at a point\nin time. Basically, it's a \"wayback machine\" that allows access to (almost)\nall past and current packages based on dates and version numbers.\n\nDebian has had snapshot archives for [10+\nyears](https://lists.debian.org/debian-announce/2010/msg00002.html). Ubuntu\nbegan providing a similar service recently and has packages available since\nMarch 1st 2023.\n\nTo use this services simply use a snapshot URL in the manifest. Here's two\nexamples showing how to do this for Debian and Ubuntu:\n  * [/examples/debian_snapshot](/examples/debian_snapshot)\n  * [/examples/ubuntu_snapshot](/examples/ubuntu_snapshot)\n\nFor more infomation, please check https://snapshot.debian.org and/or\nhttps://snapshot.ubuntu.com.","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"Name of the generated repository","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"manifest","docString":"The file used to generate the lock file","type":3,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"lock","docString":"The lock file to use for the index.","type":3,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"None","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"nolock","docString":"If you explicitly want to run without a lock, set it to `True` to avoid the DEBUG messages.","type":8,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"False","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"package_template","docString":"(EXPERIMENTAL!) a template file for generated BUILD files.","type":3,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"None","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"resolve_transitive","docString":"Whether dependencies of dependencies should be resolved and added to the lockfile.","type":8,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"True","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"mergedusr","docString":"Whether packges should be normalized following mergedusr conventions.\nTurning this on might fix the following error thrown by docker for ambigious paths: `duplicate of paths are supported.`\nFor more context please see https://salsa.debian.org/md/usrmerge/-/raw/master/debian/README.Debian?ref_type=heads","type":8,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"False","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}]}],"originKey":{"name":"","file":"//apt:extensions.bzl"}}],"repositoryRuleInfo":[],"macroInfo":[]},{"ruleInfo":[{"ruleName":"cacerts","docString":"Create a ca-certificates.crt bundle from Common CA certificates.\n\nWhen provided with the `ca-certificates` Debian package it will create a bundle\nof all common CA certificates at `/usr/share/ca-certificates` and bundle them into\na `ca-certificates.crt` file at `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`\n\nAn example of this would be\n\n```starlark\n# MODULE.bazel\nhttp_archive = use_repo_rule(\"@bazel_tools//tools/build_defs/repo:http.bzl\", \"http_archive\")\n\nhttp_archive(\n    name = \"ca-certificates\",\n    type = \".deb\",\n    sha256 = \"b2d488ad4d8d8adb3ba319fc9cb2cf9909fc42cb82ad239a26c570a2e749c389\",\n    urls = [\"https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20231106T210201Z/pool/main/c/ca-certificates/ca-certificates_20210119_all.deb\"],\n    build_file_content = \"exports_files([\"data.tar.xz\"])\"\n)\n\n# BUILD.bazel\nload(\"@rules_distroless//distroless:defs.bzl\", \"cacerts\")\n\ncacerts(\n    name = \"example\",\n    package = \"@ca-certificates//:data.tar.xz\",\n)\n```\n\nTo use the generated certificate bundle for SSL, **you must set SSL_CERT_FILE in the\nenvironment**. You can set it on the oci image like so:\n```starlark\noci_image(\n    name = \"my-image\",\n    env = {\n        \"SSL_CERT_FILE\": \"/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\",\n    }\n)\n```","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"package","docString":"","type":3,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"mode","docString":"mode for the entries","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"0555\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"time","docString":"time for the entries","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"0.0\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"cacerts","file":"//distroless/private:cacerts.bzl"}},{"ruleName":"locale","docString":"Create a locale archive from a Debian package.\n\nAn example of this would be\n\n```starlark\n# MODULE.bazel\nhttp_archive = use_repo_rule(\"@bazel_tools//tools/build_defs/repo:http.bzl\", \"http_archive\")\n\nhttp_archive(\n    name = \"libc-bin\",\n    build_file_content = 'exports_files([\"data.tar.xz\"])',\n    sha256 = \"8b048ab5c7e9f5b7444655541230e689631fd9855c384e8c4a802586d9bbc65a\",\n    urls = [\"https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian-security/20231106T230332Z/pool/updates/main/g/glibc/libc-bin_2.31-13+deb11u7_amd64.deb\"],\n)\n\n# BUILD.bazel\nload(\"@rules_distroless//distroless:defs.bzl\", \"locale\")\n\nlocale(\n    name = \"example\",\n    package = \"@libc-bin//:data.tar.xz\"\n)\n```","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"package","docString":"","type":3,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"charset","docString":"","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"C.utf8\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"time","docString":"time for the entries","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"0.0\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"locale","file":"//distroless/private:locale.bzl"}},{"ruleName":"java_keystore","docString":"Create a java keystore (database) of cryptographic keys, X.509 certificate chains, and trusted certificates.\n\nCurrently only public  X.509 are supported as part of the PUBLIC API contract.","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"certificates","docString":"","type":7,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"mode","docString":"mode for the entries","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"0755\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"time","docString":"time for the entries","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"0.0\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"java_keystore","file":"//distroless/private:java_keystore.bzl"}},{"ruleName":"flatten","docString":"Flatten multiple archives into single archive.","attribute":[{"name":"name","docString":"A unique name for this target.","type":1,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"tars","docString":"List of tars to flatten","type":7,"mandatory":true,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"deduplicate","docString":"EXPERIMENTAL: We may change or remove it without a notice.\n\nRemove duplicate entries from the archives after flattening.\nDeduplication is performed only for directories.","type":8,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"False","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false},{"name":"compress","docString":"Compress the archive file with a supported algorithm.","type":4,"mandatory":false,"providerNameGroup":[],"defaultValue":"\"\"","nonconfigurable":false,"nativelyDefined":false}],"test":false,"executable":false,"originKey":{"name":"flatten","file":"//distroless/private:flatten.bzl"}}],"providerInfo":[],"funcInfo":[{"functionName":"os_release","parameter":[{"name":"name","docString":"name of the target","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"content","docString":"a key, value dictionary that will be serialized into `=` seperated lines.\n\nSee https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/os-release.html#Options for well known keys.","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"path","docString":"where to put the file in the result archive. default: `/usr/lib/os-release`","defaultValue":"\"/usr/lib/os-release\"","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"mode","docString":"mode for the entry","defaultValue":"\"0555\"","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"time","docString":"time for the entry","defaultValue":"\"0\"","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"kwargs","docString":"other named arguments to expanded targets. see [common rule attributes](https://bazel.build/reference/be/common-definitions#common-attributes).","defaultValue":"","mandatory":false,"role":0}],"docString":"Create an Operating System Identification file from a key, value dictionary.\n\nhttps://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/os-release.html\n","originKey":{"name":"os_release","file":"//distroless/private:os_release.bzl"}},{"functionName":"group","parameter":[{"name":"name","docString":"name of the target","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"entries","docString":"an array of dicts which will be serialized into single group file.","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"time","docString":"time for the entry","defaultValue":"\"0.0\"","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"mode","docString":"mode for the entry","defaultValue":"\"0644\"","mandatory":false,"role":0},{"name":"kwargs","docString":"other named arguments to expanded targets. see [common rule attributes](https://bazel.build/reference/be/common-definitions#common-attributes).","defaultValue":"","mandatory":false,"role":0}],"docString":"Create a group file from array of dicts.\n\nhttps://www.ibm.com/docs/en/aix/7.2?topic=files-etcgroup-file#group_security__a21597b8__title__1\n","originKey":{"name":"group","file":"//distroless/private:group.bzl"}},{"functionName":"passwd","parameter":[{"name":"name","docString":"name of the target","defaultValue":"","mandatory":true,"role":0},{"name":"entries","docString":"an array of dicts which will be serialized into single passwd file.\n\nAn example;\n\n```\ndict(gid = 0, uid = 0, home = \"/root\", shell = \"/bin/bash\", username = \"root\")\n```","